    {
      "attributes": {
        "description": "Each multicast group and port seen on the network, with the number of distinct hosts sending to it and the number of hosts subscribed to it via IGMP. A sender doesn’t have to be subscribed, so more senders than participants is normal for discovery protocols like mDNS and LLMNR. Look for groups with zero participants, and for low-count rows with a single sender on a port unusual for the group. The participant list is the IGMP membership at the time Zeek logged the connection, not a full history.",
